#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"FlickrExport Kipi-plugin allows the user to upload photos to the <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.flickr.com\">Flickr</ulink> web service."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: flickrexport.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: flickrexport.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kipi"
msgstr "Kipi"

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Flickr Export"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:30
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Flickr is an online photo management application. Flickr is a way to get your "
"photos to the people who matter to you. With Flickr you can show off your "
"favorite photos to the world, blog the photos you take with a cameraphone, "
"and "
"securely and privately show photos to your friends and family around the "
"world."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The FlickrExport plugin can be used to upload an image collection from your "
"computer to the remote flickr server using the Internet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plugin initialization on first access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When accessing the plugin for the first time the user you are taken through "
"the "
"process of obtaining a token which is used for authentication purposes. The "
"following dialog will popup and a browser window will be launched you will "
"log "
"in to <ulink url=\"http://www.flickr.com\">Flickr</ulink>:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "The First Sign Up Dialog Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After successful signup FlickrUploadr will be allowed to send photos to the "
"flickr website. You will be presented with the following page on successful "
"signup:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Successful Signup Flickr page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then, simply close the browser windows and return to the host application "
"dialog. After clicking <guilabel>Yes</guilabel>, you will see the interface "
"used to upload photos to Flickr, described in the next section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid "Regular Plugin Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the flickrexport plugin is invoked for second time or later you are "
"greeted with the following dialog, which shows the current access permissions "
"the Flickr Export plugin has. The uploading process requires <quote>"
"write</quote> permissions. The plugin doesn't allow any other permissions as "
"of "
"now. You are then asked if they want to proceed with their current "
"permissions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Current Permissions Dialog preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After clicking <guibutton>Yes</guibutton>, you will see the interface to "
"upload "
"photos to Flickr."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After clicking <guibutton>No</guibutton>, the authentication process is "
"repeated."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main upload dialog is shown below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Uploading Dialog Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Add Photos</guibutton> button should be clicked once user has "
"set the other options in the dialog. After clicking this button an image "
"selector dialog opens up where you can select the photos you want to upload "
"and "
"click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>, whereupon the image uploading starts."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Tags</guilabel> field can be filled with a series of words "
"(comma "
"separated) which will be assigned as tags to the images uploaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Public</guilabel>, <guilabel>Friends</guilabel>, and <guilabel>"
"Family</guilabel> checkboxes can be checked to assign appropriate access "
"permissions to the images you upload. By default the images uploaded are "
"private."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <guilabel>Resize photos before uploading</guilabel> "
"option is selected, the photos will be resized before uploading. The values "
"will be read from the <guilabel>Maximum dimension</guilabel> combobox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Maximum Dimension</guilabel> combobox can be used to adjust the "
"maximum height to which the photos will be resized before uploading. The "
"width "
"calculation will be done so as to have the aspect ratio conserved."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: flickrexport.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Uploading Progress Dialog Preview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can click <guilabel>Cancel</guilabel> button to abort the uploading of "
"photos."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: flickrexport.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, you can view the uploaded photos by visting the <ulink "
"url=\"http://www.flickr.com\">Flickr</ulink> website."
msgstr ""

